  "narrative": "The newly delivered validation resolves the H78 PTEN-loss response deadline and closes the Cas9-activity modifier question, while leaving one new constructed-signature interaction as the main unresolved lead.  \n\nFor H78, the claim is that PTEN loss is associated with a lower dependency_composite score, i.e. stronger measured dependency, in the raw exposed-minus-comparator sense. Because H78 was registered in the negative direction, a positive signed estimate means the raw contrast is negative. The original discovery estimate was +0.239 and the independent validation is +0.285, with the validation interval signed +0.146 to +0.424. The replication direction is robust and the magnitude is roughly twice the 0.15-unit threshold. The lower independent bound is marginally below threshold, so H78 is not as unequivocally threshold-certified as the clean-context PTEN claim H104, whose validated lower bound is above 0.15. Still, the replicated point estimates and the independently validated clean conditional PTEN association support accepting H78 as a dataset-specific marginal PTEN-loss association with stronger dependency. \n\nFor the Cas9-activity modifier claims, validation weakens rather than rescues the original discovery signal. H31 claimed that the KEAP1-loss positive association is larger among high cas9_activity_score; signed validation R79 is only -0.035, with interval -0.228 to +0.158. This does not support the positive claim. H41 is the reversed claim that the KEAP1-loss effect is more negative among high cas9_activity_score; its signed validation is +0.035, with interval -0.158 to +0.228, far below the 0.15-unit threshold. I therefore keep H31 rejected and close it, and reject H41 as well. The earlier near-threshold Cas9 modifier signal is not reproduced at required confidence, and this technical/modifier avenue should not drive further allocation. \n\nThe current supported scientific picture in this dataset is an independent, largely additive central partition: KEAP1 loss is associated with higher composite dependency score; TP53 loss is associated with higher composite score; SMARCA4 loss is associated with lower composite score; and PTEN loss is associated with lower composite score. More negative scores indicate stronger dependency, so KEAP1-loss and TP53-loss cells show weaker measured dependency, while SMARCA4-loss and PTEN-loss cells show stronger measured dependency. The pairwise interaction matrix among KEAP1, TP53, SMARCA4, and PTEN is mostly null, and reverse conditioning supports the conclusion that each central association persists even after excluding the other three central losses. The main unresolved uncertainty around PTEN is that its clean TP53-loss and SMARCA4-loss contexts are directionally supportive but imprecise, although the clean all-four-negative-background PTEN claim is independently validated. \n\nThe strongest new unresolved lead is the reversed PTEN-by-research_signature_b interaction H124: the raw interaction is positive, indicating that high research_signature_b attenuates the negative PTEN-loss association. I do not accept this post-hoc reversed constructed-signature interaction yet because it requires direct validation and stratum-level characterization. The most informative next analyses are therefore PTEN-loss main effects within research_signature_b upper-quartile and lower strata, plus PTEN-by-signature_c interaction H121 to test specificity. If the high-signature_b PTEN effect is null while the low-signature_b PTEN effect is threshold-level, this would be a scientifically useful dataset-specific modifier pattern; if validation or signature_c is null, the central additive partition remains the main conclusion. All statements remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Current supported central dataset-specific partition: KEAP1 loss -> higher dependency_composite; TP53 loss -> higher dependency_composite; SMARCA4 loss -> lower dependency_composite; PTEN loss -> lower dependency_composite. More negative dependency_composite means stronger measured dependency. H78 PTEN marginal validation: signed +0.285 lower +0.146 upper +0.424. Lower bound slightly below threshold, but replicated direction/magnitude and clean H104 validation (signed +0.294 lower +0.178 upper +0.409) justify keeping H78 accepted. H17 TP53-loss among KEAP1-loss validated; H23 original positive-direction SMARCA4-loss rejected; H77 reversed SMARCA4-loss accepted. \n\nInteraction status among central predictors is largely null: KEAP1-by-TP53 null (H18), PTEN-by-KEAP1 null (H105), SMARCA4-by-TP53 not supported (H95), SMARCA4-by-KEAP1 null (H96), PTEN-by-TP53 null (H97), PTEN-by-SMARCA4 null (H98). Reverse conditioning supports independence: in PTEN-loss clean cells, KEAP1 loss H115 +0.671 lower +0.471, TP53 loss H116 +0.803 lower +0.595, and SMARCA4 loss H117 +0.790 lower +0.622 are accepted. PTEN in KEAP1-loss clean cells H119 +0.390 lower +0.202 accepted. Borderline unresolved PTEN clean contexts: TP53-loss-only H113 +0.253 lower +0.057; SMARCA4-loss-only H118 +0.227 lower +0.072. CDKN2A clean-context H123 is borderline near threshold (+0.164 lower +0.101), deferred. \n\nCas9-activity modifier resolved null: H31 and H41 now rejected/closed because independent validation R79 is near zero and not threshold-level. Do not allocate more validation to this technical modifier. \n\nPending signature interaction lead: H120 negative-direction PTEN-by-research_signature_b was rejected; raw positive interaction is +0.423 lower +0.216 upper +0.630, and reversed positive-direction claim H124 is unresolved active pending validation/characterization. Next, select H121 PTEN-by-signature_c interaction and the newly proposed PTEN-loss mean differences within research_signature_b high versus low strata. If H124 remains robust after validation and high/low strata show coherent attenuation, accept the signature_b modifier as a dataset-specific finding. If signature_c and/or validation are null, keep the main conclusion as central additive PTEN/KEAP1/TP53/SMARCA4 associations with no reliable signature modifier. Lower-priority technical, ploidy/aneuploidy/mutation-burden, KRAS, lineage/growth-pattern, media/QC, and clean MYC screens should remain deferred unless they are needed to resolve a threshold-level central or signature interaction. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims."
